   "where": "BDY-21 (class-(i) paragraph, 'it takes no cap_rects'), BDY-24 tail ('can_rebase_detach(old_body_id, frame_shift_px) is unchanged'), 3.5 BM4 checks cell, D.5 pose-range text, Edge Cases (cut beyond WORLD_COORD_LIMIT), AC-BDY-128 and its integration twin, 8.3 Assembly row ('can_rebase_detach unchanged'), Open Question 34",
   "issue": "The ADR-0015 sync added the amendment that can_rebase_detach(views, old_body_id, shift_x, shift_y, cap_rects) returns BDY_REBASE_ACTOR_IN_CAP. It left the old one-shift form, 'takes no cap_rects' and 'unchanged, so Assembly's V4 and the MSA-7 reason order are untouched' in the same rules, the 3.5 row and the ACs. BDY-24's note supersedes only 'the next sentences', and BDY-21 carries no such note. AC-BDY-128 still calls can_rebase_detach(old_body_id, (576, 96)), a call that no longer matches the signature. ADR-0015 section 9 says every cut origin's validate now runs this Body check, so the V4 'untouched' claim is false. An implementer cannot tell whether the cap guard belongs in the can_ read.",
   "fix": "Rewrite each stale mention to the ADR-0015 signature, or add a one-line 'superseded by ADR-0015 section 9' note at each of the listed places. Strike 'takes no cap_rects' and 'untouched'. Update AC-BDY-128 and the 3.5 checks cell to the five-argument call. Add one AC for can_rebase_detach returning BDY_REBASE_ACTOR_IN_CAP before any mutator runs."
  },
  {
   "where": "AC-BDY-132, final clause ('GIVEN a successful BM1, THEN it returns actor_id 1, 2, 3 in call order ... the return is an int')",
   "issue": "This contradicts the amended BDY-20, BDY-21 and the 3.5 BM1 row. A successful BM1 now returns OK (0), the allocated actor_id goes into the caller-owned PlaceResult, and the id is never the return value. A test written to this AC fails against a correct implementation. The amendment note in the same AC fixes only the negative half.",
   "fix": "Reword to: a successful BM1 returns OK (0) and writes actor_id 1, 2, 3 in call order into PlaceResult, with no per-call allocation. Add the REFUSED (1) path for a closed scope to the AC-BDY-34 or AC-BDY-132 fixtures."
  }
 ]
}
